        "text": "Explains how to map workflows for the targeted processes as they actually happen, drawing on the people who deliver services rather than on official or theoretical accounts. Describes workflow diagrams as visual representations of tasks, decisions and interactions between personas, with an example for a service delivery process and the usual diagram symbols. A BID Initiative case study from Tanzania recounts a nurse's struggle with manual immunization registers and vaccine stock, and how the initiative worked with Tanzania and Zambia to define 16 business processes for better data collection, quality and use.",
