        "text": "Advises checking whether a national digital health or eHealth strategy exists and whether a national investment planning process has been carried out, in order to identify areas of alignment and difference. A case study describes mHero, which combines iHRIS, RapidPro and OpenHIM through open standards such as HL7 FHIR within the OpenHIE framework so that ministries of health can exchange messages with health workers' mobile phones, followed by a diagram of how it integrates digital health interventions. The block ends with the opening page of Chapter 6 on linking digital health implementation to enterprise architecture, introducing its purpose and listing its tools.",
