      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out the inputs and outputs of Chapter 6 together with the 'reuse and improve' principle for digital development, which urges building on existing tools, taking modular and interoperable approaches and collaborating with other implementers. Explains that aligning digital health investments with a nationally governed enterprise architecture strengthens sustainability, scale-up and institutionalization, and points to the ITU Digital health platform handbook and OpenHIE resources where no such architecture exists.",
